{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "ROM",
  "chapter": 12,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable to God, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " your reasonable service.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And be not conformed to this world: but be ye transformed by the renewing of your mind, that ye may prove what ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that good and acceptable, and perfect will of God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For through the grace given to me, I say, to every man that is among you, not to think ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more highly than he ought to think; but to think soberly, according as God hath dealt to every man the measure of faith.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For as we have many members in one body, and all members have not the same office:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So we, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "being",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " many, are one body in Christ, and every one members one of another.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Having then gifts differing according to the grace that is given to us, whether prophecy, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let us prophesy",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " according to the proportion of faith;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or ministry, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let us wait",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " on ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "our",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ministering: or he that teacheth, on teaching:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or he that exhorteth, on exhortation: he that giveth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "let him do it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with simplicity; he that ruleth, with diligence; he that showeth mercy, with cheerfulness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love be without dissimulation. Abhor that which is evil; cleave to that which is good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " kindly affectioned one to another with brotherly love; in honor preferring one another;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not slothful in business; fervent in spirit; serving the Lord;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoicing in hope; patient in tribulation; continuing earnest in prayer;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Distributing to the necessity of saints; given to hospitality.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bless them who persecute you; bless, and curse not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rejoice with them that rejoice, and weep with them that weep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the same mind one towards another. Mind not high things, but condescend to men of low estate. Be not wise in your own conceits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Recompense to no man evil for evil. Provide things honest in the sight of all men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Dearly beloved, avenge not yourselves, but ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "rather",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " give place to wrath: for it is written, Vengeance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mine; I will repay, saith the Lord.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore if thy enemy hungereth, feed him; if he thirsteth, give him drink: for in so doing thou shalt heap coals of fire on his head.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ROM.12.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:ROM.12.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Be not overcome by evil, but overcome evil with good.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
